---
title: "CLI"
description: "Execute, explain, convert, dump, diagnose, and explore QQL with the qql command."
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

The `qql` binary is the operational interface to the same runtime used by the
SDKs.

| Command | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `qql exec "…"` | Execute one statement or inline script |
| `qql execute file.qql` | Execute a script file |
| `qql explain "…"` | Show a plan without backend execution |
| `qql connect` | Start the interactive REPL |
| `qql convert [file.json]` | Convert Qdrant REST JSON to QQL |
| `qql dump collection out.qql` | Export a collection |
| `qql doctor` | Inspect backend and embedder configuration |
| `qql version` | Print version information |

{% qqlExample title="Input for CLI examples" %}
```sql
SHOW
  COLLECTIONS;
```
{% /qqlExample %}

{% terminal title="Execute and explain" %}
qql exec --json "SHOW COLLECTIONS"
qql explain "SHOW COLLECTIONS"
{% /terminal %}

## Configuration

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `QDRANT_URL` | `http://localhost:6333` | REST or gRPC endpoint |
| `QDRANT_API_KEY` | unset | Qdrant API key |
| `EMBED_URL` | unset | OpenAI-compatible embedding endpoint |
| `EMBED_MODEL` | `all-minilm:l6-v2` | model ID |
| `EMBED_DIM` | `384` | output dimension |

Use `qql --url http://host:6333 ...` to override the configured backend for one
invocation.
